."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1910, "end": 2014, "text": "\"The USGS provided me with the resources and support necessary to pursue my research passions,\" he said."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2015, "end": 2092, "text": "\"I feel fortunate to have been a part of such a talented and dedicated team.\""}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2093, "end": 2227, "text": "Today, MacKenzie continues to work as a researcher emeritus with the USGS, mentoring the next generation of geologists and scientists."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2228, "end": 2429, "text": "His legacy serves as a reminder of the importance of continued investment in scientific research and the critical role agencies like the USGS play in advancing our understanding of the world around us."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "University of Düsseldorf", "card_ids": ["d1:c1", "d1:c2"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "researcher emeritus", "card_ids": ["d2:c1"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "Colin R MacKenzie", "scope": "work for", "claim": "Colin R MacKenzie worked for the University of Düsseldorf.", "answer": "University of Düsseldorf", "quote": "In light of these findings, it is clear that Colin R MacKenzie did, in fact, work for the University of Düsseldorf.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c2", "entity": "Colin R MacKenzie", "scope": "work for", "claim": "Colin R MacKenzie worked for the University of Düsseldorf.", "answer": "University of Düsseldorf", "quote": "Jürgen Schmid, Dean of the Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences at the University of Düsseldorf, commented, \"Colin was a valued member of our academic community, and his research expertise was a significant asset to our institution.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "Colin R. MacKenzie",